[{:db/id "q-275301/field-1/0674b229b15216f6ea870ccaaf87984357f5d6af66421aad0753c15d921d419a" :answer/id #uuid "4d83c596-8922-58f7-b59b-01eb98bb6695" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "64" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275301/field-1/a38ef12f135c1e6010d68ed21f81bc27372a73a756455b7066f6182c46018cc8" :answer/id #uuid "54316cbe-d6e6-5bb4-8380-0222f7880cd0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "32" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275301/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "df7684be-e380-5be4-8713-588231c1a449" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275301/field-1/0674b229b15216f6ea870ccaaf87984357f5d6af66421aad0753c15d921d419a" :answer-field/choices ["q-275301/field-1/0674b229b15216f6ea870ccaaf87984357f5d6af66421aad0753c15d921d419a" "q-275301/field-1/a38ef12f135c1e6010d68ed21f81bc27372a73a756455b7066f6182c46018cc8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275301/field-2/a20b3c9808c291c56ec5bfc5f0f93a856fc692714ca7ebd36c5e4bc361f7075c" :answer/id #uuid "8e6e8756-b36c-5d2e-89d4-8c4bf59b6398" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "42" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275301/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "429b7f45-8086-59a7-9e68-326ad2d2e0fc" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275301/field-2/a20b3c9808c291c56ec5bfc5f0f93a856fc692714ca7ebd36c5e4bc361f7075c" :answer-field/choices ["q-275301/field-2/a20b3c9808c291c56ec5bfc5f0f93a856fc692714ca7ebd36c5e4bc361f7075c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275301" :question/id #uuid "20eebc34-9198-5a47-9d64-b9333d3bae3f" :question/math-academy-id "q-275301" :question/problem "Let $a\\times c=2i-j$ and $b\\times c=-4i+3j.$ Find $(6a-5b)\\times (2c).$\n\n$(6a-5b)\\times (2c)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$i\\,\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$j$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the following properties of the cross product:\n\n- The cross product distributes over addition/subtraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(a\\pm b)\\times c & =a\\times c\\pm b\\times c \\\\ c\\times (a\\pm b) & =c\\times a\\pm c\\times b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The cross product is associative with respect to scalar multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda a)\\times b & =\\lambda (a\\times b) \\\\ a\\times (\\lambda b) & =\\lambda (a\\times b)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's evaluate our expression:\n\n- First, we use the distributive property:\n\n$$\n(6a-5b)\\times (2c)=(6a)\\times (2c)-(5b)\\times (2c)\n$$\n\n- Next, we factor out the scalars:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(6a)\\times (2c)-(5b)\\times (2c) & =(6\\cdot 2)(a\\times c)-(5\\cdot 2)(b\\times c) \\\\  & =12(a\\times c)-10(b\\times c)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Finally, we substitute the given values for $a\\times c$ and $b\\times c,$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12(a\\times c)-10(b\\times c) & =12(2i-j)-10(-4i+3j) \\\\  & =24i-12j+40i-30j \\\\  & =64\\,i-42\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-275301/field-1" "q-275301/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e3b9100-91b5-59ec-8676-832893b05ebb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-275301"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-19767/selection/5e9855d98414e1265daa7e0283996a3f8250d9f2695c61d917b4e2a0bd12343e" :answer/id #uuid "ef3d7d1c-0032-519b-a71a-c160508c6aa0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36i-8j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19767/selection/d0ffac475ad5e1889c899fc7b28239425d1c2b80ab6a50136b0b4bd51f325196" :answer/id #uuid "23c4c533-ed16-583e-a7c6-be95c7135341" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "66i+32j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19767/selection/2a155c0d392db5bd16079ec235b04aa4a71c0c77c35e9c64a9f8a86c5ad7aebd" :answer/id #uuid "269ecffd-a72c-57a9-a35c-70916a05a5e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6i+32j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19767/selection/e1c8a3497dc1e80a298fb3261e88745ac758fdbe8f74a31602265a7c4f7df0cc" :answer/id #uuid "cf1f6623-4c90-5af4-8092-d3024b2f7f2d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "66i+8j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19767/selection/b712f4b6e43b99b4b382a14cc64c1a082fa786d6dd7f3eed2f001a5d20fbb7da" :answer/id #uuid "88dc1117-25c9-5a17-8757-8efe72efebc0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-66i-8j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19767/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a7abe480-d2e9-5e65-9843-1d8efe78bac7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-19767/selection/e1c8a3497dc1e80a298fb3261e88745ac758fdbe8f74a31602265a7c4f7df0cc" :answer-field/choices ["q-19767/selection/5e9855d98414e1265daa7e0283996a3f8250d9f2695c61d917b4e2a0bd12343e" "q-19767/selection/d0ffac475ad5e1889c899fc7b28239425d1c2b80ab6a50136b0b4bd51f325196" "q-19767/selection/2a155c0d392db5bd16079ec235b04aa4a71c0c77c35e9c64a9f8a86c5ad7aebd" "q-19767/selection/e1c8a3497dc1e80a298fb3261e88745ac758fdbe8f74a31602265a7c4f7df0cc" "q-19767/selection/b712f4b6e43b99b4b382a14cc64c1a082fa786d6dd7f3eed2f001a5d20fbb7da"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-19767" :question/id #uuid "701e8fab-0f0f-50a4-80d8-aaa5fa31fdfd" :question/math-academy-id "q-19767" :question/problem "Find $(3a-5b)\\times (2c)$, if $a\\times c=6i-2j$ and $b\\times c=-3i-2j.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the following properties of the cross product:\n\n- The cross product distributes over addition/subtraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(a\\pm b)\\times c & =a\\times c\\pm b\\times c \\\\ c\\times (a\\pm b) & =c\\times a\\pm c\\times b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The cross product is associative with respect to scalar multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda a)\\times b & =\\lambda (a\\times b) \\\\ a\\times (\\lambda b) & =\\lambda (a\\times b)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's evaluate our expression:\n\n- First, we use distributive property:\n\n$$\n(3a-5b)\\times (2c)=(3a)\\times (2c)-(5b)\\times (2c)\n$$\n\n- Next, we factor out the scalars:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3a)\\times (2c)-(5b)\\times (2c) & =(3\\cdot 2)(a\\times c)-(5\\cdot 2)(b\\times c) \\\\  & =6(a\\times c)-10(b\\times c)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Finally, we substitute the given values for $a\\times c$ and $b\\times c,$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6(a\\times c)-10(b\\times c) & =6(6i-2j)-10(-3i-2j) \\\\  & =36i-12j+30i+20j \\\\  & =66i+8j.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-19767/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e3b9100-91b5-59ec-8676-832893b05ebb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-19767"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-280351/field-1/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce" :answer/id #uuid "ace6d3dc-f2e2-5972-a0da-83cd598ddc7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-280351/field-1/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "1e94120d-331e-54a6-9588-035de8084635" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-280351/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "c63751f5-6830-589a-8a43-9ab5e839fe1b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-280351/field-1/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce" :answer-field/choices ["q-280351/field-1/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce" "q-280351/field-1/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-280351" :question/id #uuid "3efb4a72-0c3f-589b-9b0a-e3fc24ad83c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-280351" :question/problem "Let $c\\times a=3i-2j$ and $c\\times b=4i+j.$ Find $c\\times (a+2b).$\n\n$c\\times (a+2b)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$i$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the following properties of the cross product:\n\n- The cross product distributes over addition/subtraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(a\\pm b)\\times c & =a\\times c\\pm b\\times c \\\\ c\\times (a\\pm b) & =c\\times a\\pm c\\times b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The cross product is associative with respect to scalar multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda a)\\times b & =\\lambda (a\\times b) \\\\ a\\times (\\lambda b) & =\\lambda (a\\times b)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's evaluate our expression:\n\n- First, we use the distributive property:\n\n$$\nc\\times (a+2b)=c\\times a+c\\times (2b)\n$$\n\n- Next, we factor out the scalars:\n\n$$\nc\\times a+c\\times (2b)=c\\times a+2(c\\times b)\n$$\n\n- Finally, we substitute the given values for $c\\times a$ and $c\\times b,$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\times a+2(c\\times b) & =(3i-2j)+2(4i+j) \\\\  & =3i-2j+8i+2j \\\\  & =11\\,i\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-280351/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e3b9100-91b5-59ec-8676-832893b05ebb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-280351"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-19764/selection/063af3a1a6dee903729e80e71f2f92cd5aaec449e9fa97b1b1290b4a712ecce1" :answer/id #uuid "3ffc0489-23d0-5958-8239-a03bd3787001" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19764/selection/0d8188629d82a60488371fe9628bc242256e9519ad499c81244363f3d18f1b44" :answer/id #uuid "97186ea7-bc0e-5b19-9868-d661dda95bc2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8i" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19764/selection/696d182b62f9d4be2860756b65037c36bbe3b34ccac624ac940aa17828f5cdb2" :answer/id #uuid "559b89b5-4a63-59a6-be31-023b03496e72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19764/selection/4ad7a0175da18f3b2aaea2eefcbe894248d0b26c5e1ab46f92a76adfafeed8e2" :answer/id #uuid "fe7ac257-d72d-51cf-9bc4-84e7e3a1b6fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16i+6j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19764/selection/9255c26cc333e0bff7ebfe0d14b3e45f138f072d88f0b7e62c26452cdb5a9fd4" :answer/id #uuid "bdd2d8c2-0518-5d12-b38c-b2dae4a2ea52" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8i+6j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19764/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "99e2892c-21b3-5283-b79d-ed1fed6e698e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-19764/selection/063af3a1a6dee903729e80e71f2f92cd5aaec449e9fa97b1b1290b4a712ecce1" :answer-field/choices ["q-19764/selection/063af3a1a6dee903729e80e71f2f92cd5aaec449e9fa97b1b1290b4a712ecce1" "q-19764/selection/0d8188629d82a60488371fe9628bc242256e9519ad499c81244363f3d18f1b44" "q-19764/selection/696d182b62f9d4be2860756b65037c36bbe3b34ccac624ac940aa17828f5cdb2" "q-19764/selection/4ad7a0175da18f3b2aaea2eefcbe894248d0b26c5e1ab46f92a76adfafeed8e2" "q-19764/selection/9255c26cc333e0bff7ebfe0d14b3e45f138f072d88f0b7e62c26452cdb5a9fd4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-19764" :question/id #uuid "05fdfa3b-4f69-5675-a164-c998951035c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-19764" :question/problem "Find $(a+4b)\\times c$, if $a\\times c=8i+2j$ and $b\\times c=-2i+j.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the following properties of the cross product:\n\n- The cross product distributes over addition/subtraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(a\\pm b)\\times c & =a\\times c\\pm b\\times c \\\\ c\\times (a\\pm b) & =c\\times a\\pm c\\times b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The cross product is associative with respect to scalar multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda a)\\times b & =\\lambda (a\\times b) \\\\ a\\times (\\lambda b) & =\\lambda (a\\times b)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's evaluate our expression:\n\n- First, we use distributive property:\n\n$$\n(a+4b)\\times c=a\\times c+(4b)\\times c\n$$\n\n- Next, we factor out the scalars:\n  \n\n$$\na\\times c+(4b)\\times c=a\\times c+4(b\\times c)\n$$\n\n- Finally, we substitute the given values for $a\\times c$ and $b\\times c,$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times c+4(b\\times c) & =(8i+2j)+4(-2i+j) \\\\  & =8i+2j-8i+4j \\\\  & =6j.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-19764/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e3b9100-91b5-59ec-8676-832893b05ebb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-19764"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-275297/field-1/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "f6c481ca-f968-5207-a16e-6ab88d35af3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275297/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "66d8fb6f-cdac-5319-ac33-2731d6f4306f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275297/field-1/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer-field/choices ["q-275297/field-1/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275297/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "71ef320b-cb71-59eb-b67f-1030f1571461" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275297/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "7843defb-963e-58c6-b5a2-289b14597a3f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275297/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-275297/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275297" :question/id #uuid "e97b870f-ee61-5999-90e7-7c284335223a" :question/math-academy-id "q-275297" :question/problem "Let $a\\times c=3i+j$ and $b\\times c=2i+2j.$ Find $(4a-3b)\\times c.$\n\n$(4a-3b)\\times c=$\n{{field-1}}\n$i\\,\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$j$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the following properties of the cross product:\n\n- The cross product distributes over addition/subtraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(a\\pm b)\\times c & =a\\times c\\pm b\\times c \\\\ c\\times (a\\pm b) & =c\\times a\\pm c\\times b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The cross product is associative with respect to scalar multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda a)\\times b & =\\lambda (a\\times b) \\\\ a\\times (\\lambda b) & =\\lambda (a\\times b)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's evaluate our expression:\n\n- First, we use the distributive property:\n\n$$\n(4a-3b)\\times c=(4a)\\times c-(3b)\\times c\n$$\n\n- Next, we factor out the scalars:\n\n$$\n(4a)\\times c-(3b)\\times c=4(a\\times c)-3(b\\times c)\n$$\n\n- Finally, we substitute the given values for $a\\times c$ and $b\\times c,$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(a\\times c)-3(b\\times c) & =4(3i+j)-3(2i+2j) \\\\  & =12i+4j-6i-6j \\\\  & =6\\,i-2\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-275297/field-1" "q-275297/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e3b9100-91b5-59ec-8676-832893b05ebb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-275297"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-127858"] :question/problem "Find $(7a-2b)\\times b$, if $b\\times a=⟨2,-1,6⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the following properties of the cross product:\n\n- The cross product distributes over addition/subtraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(a\\pm b)\\times c & =a\\times c\\pm b\\times c \\\\ c\\times (a\\pm b) & =c\\times a\\pm c\\times b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The cross product is associative with respect to scalar multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda a)\\times b & =\\lambda (a\\times b) \\\\ a\\times (\\lambda b) & =\\lambda (a\\times b)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The cross product of parallel vectors equals the zero vector. In particular,\n\n$$\na\\times a=0.\n$$\n\n- The cross product is anticommutative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =-b\\times a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's evaluate our expression:\n\n- First, we use the distributive property:\n\n$$\n(7a-2b)\\times b=(7a)\\times b-(2b)\\times b\n$$\n\n- Next, we factor out the scalars:\n\n$$\n(7a)\\times b-(2b)\\times b=7(a\\times b)-2(b\\times b)\n$$\n\n- Then, we use anticommutativity, and the fact that $b\\times b=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(a\\times b)-2(b\\times b) & =7(-b\\times a)-2(0) \\\\  & =-7(b\\times a)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Substitute the given value for $b\\times a$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-7(b\\times a) & =-7⟨2,-1,6⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-14,7,-42⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-280385/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "4ca84640-a7cb-5896-a131-6ecee08c95ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-280385/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "1dad7791-a4c2-5989-9982-b2d44f86c4ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-280385/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d18aaa03-ddae-5e56-8ba8-63e6f0339b61" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-280385/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer-field/choices ["q-280385/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-280385/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-280385/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "9e191b4c-b08c-570d-bdcd-6cb98f684543" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-280385/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "ddecc61e-b6b5-5aa2-b24f-9c579608af40" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-280385/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-280385/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-280385/field-3/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "07e2a6c6-938e-5c53-be36-de98b5f3e77a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-280385/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "590347d9-f78d-5d7b-bf89-cac6a0147fd9" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-280385/field-3/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer-field/choices ["q-280385/field-3/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-280385" :question/id #uuid "b7ee41b4-1ee9-5318-a7d3-51caf796ea0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-280385" :question/problem "Let $b\\times a=2i-j+4k.$ Find $a\\times (b-3a).$\n\n$a\\times (b-3a)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$i\\,\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$j\\,\\,+$\n{{field-3}}\n$k$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the following properties of the cross product:\n\n- The cross product distributes over addition/subtraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(a\\pm b)\\times c & =a\\times c\\pm b\\times c \\\\ c\\times (a\\pm b) & =c\\times a\\pm c\\times b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The cross product is associative with respect to scalar multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda a)\\times b & =\\lambda (a\\times b) \\\\ a\\times (\\lambda b) & =\\lambda (a\\times b)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The cross product of parallel vectors equals the zero vector. In particular,\n\n$$\na\\times a=0\n$$\n\n- The cross product is anticommutative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =-b\\times a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's evaluate our expression:\n\n- First, we use the distributive property:\n\n$$\na\\times (b-3a)=a\\times b-a\\times (3a)\n$$\n\n- Next, we factor out the scalars:\n\n$$\na\\times b-a\\times (3a)=a\\times b-3(a\\times a)\n$$\n\n- Then, we use the anticommutativity property and the fact that $a\\times a=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b-3(a\\times a) & =-b\\times a-3(0) \\\\  & =-b\\times a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Substitute the given value for $b\\times a$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-b\\times a & =-(2i-j+4k) \\\\  & =-2i+1j+-4k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-280385/field-1" "q-280385/field-2" "q-280385/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "88c81beb-9b15-56ae-bb46-ce5cbc1d0ea5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-280385"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-280834/field-1/594f4371237f716a4e7b771cfac6a2ca8b8eb3c8dcb7752f2b3291728275476a" :answer/id #uuid "b265f3ba-66e0-5ba8-a951-f22bbd1dd471" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-280834/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "eee3e1c6-c51d-5cc6-8a76-61f3b3cd01d9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-280834/field-1/594f4371237f716a4e7b771cfac6a2ca8b8eb3c8dcb7752f2b3291728275476a" :answer-field/choices ["q-280834/field-1/594f4371237f716a4e7b771cfac6a2ca8b8eb3c8dcb7752f2b3291728275476a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-280834/field-2/23a7b929cccc5bdeb88db3bdc770afbaf59570d63e930fc5c94f26cb6f5091dc" :answer/id #uuid "c0832071-e3c0-5c36-9be9-8eb356b104f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "60" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-280834/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "8b2a7e63-4f9b-5d83-a67e-d21e73372bc4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-280834/field-2/23a7b929cccc5bdeb88db3bdc770afbaf59570d63e930fc5c94f26cb6f5091dc" :answer-field/choices ["q-280834/field-2/23a7b929cccc5bdeb88db3bdc770afbaf59570d63e930fc5c94f26cb6f5091dc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-280834/field-3/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "bce71f98-0aa2-539e-85a4-bbea8fa55b87" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-280834/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "2f745a8c-23d2-571f-8f69-6c9153835db2" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-280834/field-3/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer-field/choices ["q-280834/field-3/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-280834" :question/id #uuid "eb2f7dd6-c1c9-5720-995f-2d0f1b1202c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-280834" :question/problem "Let $a\\times b=⟨2,-5,-1⟩.$ Find $6b\\times (2a-b).$\n\n$6b\\times (2a-b)=⟨$\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the following properties of the cross product:\n\n- The cross product distributes over addition/subtraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(a\\pm b)\\times c & =a\\times c\\pm b\\times c \\\\ c\\times (a\\pm b) & =c\\times a\\pm c\\times b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The cross product is associative with respect to scalar multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda a)\\times b & =\\lambda (a\\times b) \\\\ a\\times (\\lambda b) & =\\lambda (a\\times b)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The cross product of parallel vectors equals the zero vector. In particular,\n\n$$\na\\times a=0.\n$$\n\n- The cross product is anticommutative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =-b\\times a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's evaluate our expression:\n\n- First, we use the distributive property:\n\n$$\n6b\\times (2a-b)=(6b)\\times (2a)-(6b)\\times b\n$$\n\n- Next, we factor out the scalars:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(6b)\\times (2a)-(6b)\\times b & =(6\\cdot 2)(b\\times a)-6(b\\times b) \\\\  & =12(b\\times a)-6(b\\times b)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Then, we use anticommutativity, and the fact that $b\\times b=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12(b\\times a)-6(b\\times b) & =12(-a\\times b)-6(0) \\\\  & =-12(a\\times b)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Substitute the given value for $a\\times b$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-12(a\\times b) & =-12⟨2,-5,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-24,60,12⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-280834/field-1" "q-280834/field-2" "q-280834/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "88c81beb-9b15-56ae-bb46-ce5cbc1d0ea5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-280834"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-216349/selection/ca53fa41918d7a81e1415c84bda3a7517c3a3f7827267742ff275241c94d54f0" :answer/id #uuid "60dda674-8399-5c78-a5c1-0c7d70f0bdfe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3i-6j+3k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-216349/selection/d77dccb436c28bc628155da5535d4b3ae6e597472d506e2f3198e6d51d837cfb" :answer/id #uuid "8d33d3ba-1786-58fc-ba1e-ca2a7f66f79e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-i+3j-3k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-216349/selection/15f50bb7d3f4ce22acf84b7ae817ea1fcf3b79d4ea13de87674651a15d2b4678" :answer/id #uuid "1bfa8864-943d-51b0-9897-4854ea617ced" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3i+6j-k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-216349/selection/6ecaf2a6c9ac593f8b3107e42793f0e142d79dc7af41c5f596593dc611ad14ff" :answer/id #uuid "17f6cfe7-32bb-5095-9076-eea49aebf704" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3i-9j+6k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-216349/selection/9bb70019b62771aeed53e4aee1deff614f87c5f947776f9aafc4c9e2e8baa382" :answer/id #uuid "f58e0007-2a0d-50db-93aa-8cac30b04ad6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "i-j+6k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-216349/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8ac9eae1-c568-5c6b-bf33-75adada816f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-216349/selection/ca53fa41918d7a81e1415c84bda3a7517c3a3f7827267742ff275241c94d54f0" :answer-field/choices ["q-216349/selection/ca53fa41918d7a81e1415c84bda3a7517c3a3f7827267742ff275241c94d54f0" "q-216349/selection/d77dccb436c28bc628155da5535d4b3ae6e597472d506e2f3198e6d51d837cfb" "q-216349/selection/15f50bb7d3f4ce22acf84b7ae817ea1fcf3b79d4ea13de87674651a15d2b4678" "q-216349/selection/6ecaf2a6c9ac593f8b3107e42793f0e142d79dc7af41c5f596593dc611ad14ff" "q-216349/selection/9bb70019b62771aeed53e4aee1deff614f87c5f947776f9aafc4c9e2e8baa382"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-216349" :question/id #uuid "5737be10-9d80-5366-9119-ed9296b0b909" :question/math-academy-id "q-216349" :question/problem "Find $a\\times (2a+3b)$, if $b\\times a=-i+2j-k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the following properties of the cross product:\n\n- The cross product distributes over addition/subtraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(a\\pm b)\\times c & =a\\times c\\pm b\\times c \\\\ c\\times (a\\pm b) & =c\\times a\\pm c\\times b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The cross product is associative with respect to scalar multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda a)\\times b & =\\lambda (a\\times b) \\\\ a\\times (\\lambda b) & =\\lambda (a\\times b)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The cross product of parallel vectors equals the zero vector. In particular,\n\n$$\na\\times a=0.\n$$\n\n- The cross product is anticommutative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =-b\\times a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's evaluate our expression:\n\n- First, we use the distributive property:\n\n$$\na\\times (2a+3b)=a\\times (2a)+a\\times (3b)\n$$\n\n- Next, we factor out the scalars:\n\n$$\na\\times (2a)+a\\times (3b)=2(a\\times a)+3(a\\times b)\n$$\n\n- Then, we use anticommutativity, and the fact that $a\\times a=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(a\\times a)+3(a\\times b) & =2(0)+3(-b\\times a) \\\\  & =-3(b\\times a)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Substitute the given value for $b\\times a$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3(b\\times a) & =-3(-i+2j-k) \\\\  & =3i-6j+3k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-216349/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "88c81beb-9b15-56ae-bb46-ce5cbc1d0ea5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-216349"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-280381/field-1/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "825fffe4-09ee-59c6-ad77-043f41ac4d63" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-280381/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "5e325e0a-b297-5c07-a86c-0b5eb206432f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-280381/field-1/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer-field/choices ["q-280381/field-1/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-280381/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "02c9444b-b5eb-54bc-8c62-4f221eb46c12" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-280381/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "74c8d7a8-4a25-511a-9dd6-20ef55196b0f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-280381/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-280381/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-280381/field-3/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer/id #uuid "5ae9c36d-193d-5fa9-8a02-3ff832b4d7ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-280381/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "d60586f6-b5de-5eb9-8751-b98c56fde987" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-280381/field-3/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer-field/choices ["q-280381/field-3/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-280381" :question/id #uuid "06dea262-c0fb-5771-98be-7872614d7182" :question/math-academy-id "q-280381" :question/problem "Let $b\\times a=⟨6,0,-3⟩.$ Find $a\\times (3a-2b).$\n\n$a\\times (3a-2b)=⟨$\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the following properties of the cross product:\n\n- The cross product distributes over addition/subtraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(a\\pm b)\\times c & =a\\times c\\pm b\\times c \\\\ c\\times (a\\pm b) & =c\\times a\\pm c\\times b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The cross product is associative with respect to scalar multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda a)\\times b & =\\lambda (a\\times b) \\\\ a\\times (\\lambda b) & =\\lambda (a\\times b)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The cross product of parallel vectors equals the zero vector. In particular,\n\n$$\na\\times a=0\n$$\n\n- The cross product is anticommutative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =-b\\times a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's evaluate our expression:\n\n- First, we use the distributive property:\n\n$$\na\\times (3a-2b)=a\\times (3a)-a\\times (2b)\n$$\n\n- Next, we factor out the scalars:\n\n$$\na\\times (3a)-a\\times (2b)=3(a\\times a)-2(a\\times b)\n$$\n\n- Then, we use the anticommutativity property and the fact that $a\\times a=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(a\\times a)-2(a\\times b) & =3(0)-2(-b\\times a) \\\\  & =2(b\\times a)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Substitute the given value for $b\\times a$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(b\\times a) & =2⟨6,0,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨12,0,-6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-280381/field-1" "q-280381/field-2" "q-280381/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "88c81beb-9b15-56ae-bb46-ce5cbc1d0ea5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-280381"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-14746"] :question/problem "Find $(-2\\mathbf{a}+5\\mathbf{b}) \\times \\mathbf{c},$ if $\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{c} = \\mathbf{i}$ and $\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c} = -3\\mathbf{i}+\\mathbf{j}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the following properties of the cross product:\n\n- The cross product distributes over addition/subtraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(a\\pm b)\\times c & =a\\times c\\pm b\\times c \\\\ c\\times (a\\pm b) & =c\\times a\\pm c\\times b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The cross product is associative with respect to scalar multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda a)\\times b & =\\lambda (a\\times b) \\\\ a\\times (\\lambda b) & =\\lambda (a\\times b)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's evaluate our expression:\n\n- First, we use distributive property:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2a+5b)\\times c & =(-2a)\\times c+(5b)\\times c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we factor out the scalars:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2a)\\times c+(5b)\\times c & =-2(a\\times c)+5(b\\times c)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Finally, we substitute the given values for $\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{c}$ and $\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c},$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2(a\\times c)+5(b\\times c) & =-2\\cdot (i)+5\\cdot (-3i+j) \\\\  & =-2i-15i+5j \\\\  & =-17i+5j\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-14747"] :question/problem "Find $2\\mathbf{a} \\times (\\mathbf{a}+3\\mathbf{b})$, if $\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{a} = \\mathbf{i}-\\mathbf{j}-2 \\mathbf{k}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the following properties of the cross product:\n\n- The cross product distributes over addition/subtraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(a\\pm b)\\times c & =a\\times c\\pm b\\times c \\\\ c\\times (a\\pm b) & =c\\times a\\pm c\\times b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The cross product is associative with respect to scalar multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda a)\\times b & =\\lambda (a\\times b) \\\\ a\\times (\\lambda b) & =\\lambda (a\\times b)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The cross product of parallel vectors equals the zero vector. In particular,\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{a} = \\mathbf{0}.\n$$\n\n- The cross product is anticommutative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =-b\\times a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's evaluate our expression:\n\n- First, we use the distributive property:\n\n$$\n2\\mathbf{a} \\times (\\mathbf{a}+3\\mathbf{b})=( 2\\mathbf{a}) \\times (\\mathbf{a}) + (2\\mathbf{a}) \\times (3\\mathbf{b})\n$$\n\n- Next, we factor out the scalars:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2a)\\times (a)+(2a)\\times (3b) & =2(a\\times a)+(2\\cdot 3)(a\\times b) \\\\  & =2(a\\times a)+6(a\\times b)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Then, we use anticommutativity, and the fact that $\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{a} = \\mathbf{0}{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(a\\times a)+6(a\\times b) & =2(0)+6(-b\\times a) \\\\  & =-6(b\\times a)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Finally, we substitute the given value for $\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{a}$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6(b\\times a) & =-6(i-j-2k) \\\\  & =-6i+6j+12k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
